  "id": "secondary-symptoms",
  "term": "secondary symptoms",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, secondary symptoms are changes found along with a disorder that may result from it rather than produce it. The passage uses the term for bodily changes, such as common pathological findings, whose role as cause is doubtful.",
